#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114952 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115368 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f61a7c3-82e6-5f90-8a95-4a79078fd542" :knowledge-point/title "Vertical Reflections of Exponential Growth Functions"}] :question/id #uuid "5e2f19a2-f9e3-59dd-83a9-90950b0a55a8" :question/math-academy-id "e-20883" :question/problem "Plot the graph of $y=-2(7^x)-1.$" :question/worked-solution "To plot the given function, we follow these steps:\n\n- We take the curve $y=2(7^x).$\n\n![](images/08/088e67a4b4d49a0e26d01f473e1513bce26c146da4173ada9d6b401f411253cd.png)\n\n- Reflect it on the $x$-axis to give $y=-2(7^x).$ The $y$-intercept moves from $(0,2)$ to $(0,-2)$ but the horizontal asymptote stays at $y=0.$\n\n![](images/48/48d991aa81c055a890199355e88c28a8ec178411687ebc260eec50e70718a72a.png)\n\n- Then, vertically shift it by $1$ unit down to give $y=-2(7^x)-1.$ The point $(0,-2)$ moves to $(0,-3)$ and the horizontal asymptote moves from $y=0$ to $y=-1.$\n\n![](images/7e/7e44e7df0372c67db670abd63706c316560a226bd3f63dc8f9c0ca104342128c.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114953 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115369 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "623f4440-ba1a-58ce-9ff2-ccdf591a0d30" :knowledge-point/title "Vertical Reflections of Exponential Decay Functions"}] :question/id #uuid "0ab5addd-b4b1-56b8-8cd2-690d5be81b8a" :question/math-academy-id "e-20884" :question/problem "Plot the graph of $y = -\\left( \\dfrac 12 \\right)^x + 2.$" :question/worked-solution "To plot the given function, we follow these steps:\n\n- We take the curve $y=\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)^{x}.$\n\n![](images/e9/e9331b26e26b99d3d8fcaea0bb7864b45f697211d3f30c41e9cc5329b1ef5d45.png)\n\n- Reflect it on the $x$-axis to give $y=-\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)^{x}.$ The $y$-intercept moves from $(0,1)$ to $(0,-1)$ but the horizontal asymptote stays at $y=0.$\n\n![](images/df/df29fef3da108d38afc6a0275cc8b0f52237915576a8d7528f90ffeab5588264.png)\n\n- Then, vertically shift it by $2$ units up to give $y=-\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)^{x}+2.$ The point $(0,-1)$ moves to $(0,1)$ and the horizontal asymptote moves from from $y=0$ to $y=2.$\n\n![](images/e6/e63aa682e19fef317badd419805ffd82a449559a159a41650d2260daf33eff76.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390645 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115368 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f61a7c3-82e6-5f90-8a95-4a79078fd542" :knowledge-point/title "Vertical Reflections of Exponential Growth Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a771d975-2aaa-513d-bcb8-8905d9edc2ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/55/5559cd21367ed24058d7f0a3f1f646feb6cbdc269cbd4128788b17cbd331a01e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390647} {:answer/id #uuid "41d7c55e-75b0-54d8-907f-70f90a5594aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b0/b05cb7e1d42380d1a1ac76139b39bbed49f429dbc43fddbae79b47e61d5659fd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390648} {:answer/id #uuid "1dd1f9e6-af1e-5909-94b9-5f25d90a06ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/30/30b885e19455654b28e87aba56427a82bfb9abe98d28dc5b542214a7fd55315f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390649} {:answer/id #uuid "bb4ddff0-6b9c-5567-88cf-552367429984" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/7f/7fbb4a84bc3fa077711d003c7b05fa8bccfb84b31a112736363fa4de00315e54.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390650} {:answer/id #uuid "b0ef6180-669c-546a-a8a2-ed7f728e356b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/78/7868ed246bfad0cbcb848098c39443616acf8554620537ad5cf53fa46fdaf9e0.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390651}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1dd1f9e6-af1e-5909-94b9-5f25d90a06ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/30/30b885e19455654b28e87aba56427a82bfb9abe98d28dc5b542214a7fd55315f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390649} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9df4524-7dfb-5370-9bcc-d5a8bffd76f2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390646}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d6b5ac66-3c43-5e20-bd0d-692b07d708ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-317281" :question/problem "Which of the following is the graph of $y=-{3}^{x}+1?$" :question/worked-solution "To plot the given function, we follow these steps:\n\n- We take the curve $y={3}^{x}.$\n\n![](images/17/17a76468bd4f446f420d784ae479724135b2af3369a7d69f87c67507e74a8901.png)\n\n- Reflect it on the $x$-axis to give $y=-{3}^{x}.$ The $y$-intercept moves from $(0,1)$ to $(0,-1)$ but the horizontal asymptote stays at $y=0.$\n\n![](images/ac/ac5e769c069b753bbf3f6a9a276b69881a3d2699afc4f62498233ecc526f5a2b.png)\n\n- Then, vertically shift it by $1$ unit up to give $y=-{3}^{x}+1.$ The point $(0,-1)$ moves to $(0,0)$ and the horizontal asymptote moves from $y=0$ to $y=1.$\n\n![](images/c6/c69c8be5828709cef483cba56d5842b973cf718e7592a8fba9e825be08204f5b.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299595 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115369 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "623f4440-ba1a-58ce-9ff2-ccdf591a0d30" :knowledge-point/title "Vertical Reflections of Exponential Decay Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "162becf1-1bd4-584f-967c-51eeb7d6032b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/de/defd4e44b6a4f65bdca693609e76936df5577963129262673866fbcd970b51af.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297648} {:answer/id #uuid "781c642e-4551-52d5-8d96-d883025d7107" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/9